Flann sprite integration

The first roster slot uses the canonical flann ID and the exact v_flann.PNG asset.
The shared Canvas drawCar path renders the same artwork in the showroom, garage,
normal races and local split screen. Keep the other five procedural car models.

Load the image once; repaint previews when it loads. Use natural image dimensions,
normalized visible bounds and one uniform scale. Draw shadow, anchored exhaust,
then the full image. Tailpipe anchors are normalized source coordinates, shared
by every view; pulse smoothly and stay static with reduced motion enabled.

Only the six-racer field belongs on the road. Keep racer AI, collision consequences, hazards,
items, Conditions, finish/results, local play, saved distance and all performance
tuning unchanged. Remove the dormant non-racer road-vehicle subsystem entirely.

Validation commands:
node tools/check.mjs
node tools/menu-check.mjs
node tools/ultimate-check.mjs
node tools/sprite-check.mjs
node tools/hitbox-check.mjs

Follow-up: use precise shared body hitboxes for players and bots. Exclude image
padding, shadows and exhaust; rotate with the car. Rear contacts require actual
body overlap, and hazard contact must follow the visible hazard shape.

Implementation and validation details: docs/FLANN-QA.md.
